### Product CRUD. Switch @host between the two apps; both behave the same.
### Data lives in PostgreSQL (profile local = 5433, docker = 5432): the day-1 catalog has 12 products.
### Delete is a soft delete, so SKUs are never freed: change @sku before re-running create.

@host = http://localhost:8080
# @host = http://localhost:8000
@sku = TST-1001

### 1. List products: first page of 20 -> {items, page, size, totalItems, totalPages}
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products

### 1b. Second page of 5 (page is 0-based; size 1-100)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?page=1&size=5

### 2. Create a product: 201 Created + Location header
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "{{sku}}",
  "name": "Coffee mug",
  "description": "Ceramic, 350 ml",
  "price": "12.50"
}

### 3. Same SKU again: 409 Conflict
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "{{sku}}",
  "name": "Another mug",
  "price": "9.99"
}

### 4. Get one by id: 200 (id 1 is the day-1 coffee mug; use the id from step 2 for yours)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products/1

### 5. Update name, price and status (the SKU can't change): 200. Put your product's id here
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/products/13
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Large coffee mug",
  "description": "Ceramic, 500 ml",
  "price": "14.50",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### 6. Delete (soft delete -> status DISCONTINUED): 204 No Content
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/products/13

### 7. Get after delete: 200, status DISCONTINUED
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products/13
